Hi folks,

I'm trying to put together a recipe to include llvm and clang in the yocto =
toolchain.  My goal is to have the clang compiler available for application=
 development.  I do not intend to compile the kernel or OS image with clang=
.  I have created a recipe and placed it in one of my added layers as follo=
ws:

LICENSE =3D "NCSA"
PR =3D "r0"
LIC_FILES_CHKSUM =3D "file://LICENSE.TXT;md5=3D47e311aa9caedd1b3abf098bd781=
4d1d"

SRC_URI =3D "file://llvm-3.5.0.tar.gz \
          "
SRC_URI[md5sum] =3D "e2dd127722ffb305c981d2a02687b4ff"
SRC_URI[sha256sum] =3D "1badb762129feb7ced9484a7969c88cebab9b01b80b83002fc9=
690933cd7d0e0"

EXTRA_OECONF =3D "--config=3DLinux-yocto "

INHIBIT_PACKAGE_DEBUG_SPLIT =3D "1"

INSANE_SKIP_${PN} =3D "already-stripped"

#FILES_${PN} =3D "${libdir}/* /usr/bin "
inherit autotools

do_configure () {
        ./configure --enable-optimized --enable-targets=3Dx86,x86_64 --host=
=3Dx86_64-unknown-linux-gnu --build=3Dx86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
}

The recipe is copied from another recipe of mine that builds the POCO libra=
ries, so INSANE_SKIP_${PN} =3D "already-stripped" may not actually be neces=
sary, but was left in until I got the recipe running.

I add the recipe to the toolchain by including it in TOOLCHAIN_HOST_TASK fr=
om my local.conf, thus:
"TOOLCHAIN_HOST_TASK +=3D " llvm "

This gets the source unpacked, configures, and compiles, but do_install fai=
ls with several instances of this message: "ERROR: ld.so: object 'libpseudo=
.so' from LD_PRELOAD cannot be preloaded: ignored."

Even though it doesn't install, the build products are in the work director=
y, so I examined them.

[jimr@krusty llvm-3.5.0]$ file /home/jimr/tera/yocto/daisy/build/tmp/work/i=
586-poky-linux/llvm/3.5.0-r0/llvm-3.5.0/Release+Asserts/bin/clang
/home/jimr/tera/yocto/daisy/build/tmp/work/i586-poky-linux/llvm/3.5.0-r0/ll=
vm-3.5.0/Release+Asserts/bin/clang: ELF 32-bit LSB executable, Intel 80386,=
 version 1 (SYSV), dynamically linked (uses shared libs), for GNU/Linux 2.6=
.16, BuildID[sha1]=3D0x96bd97125551d23e94bcbbc4e68b69b8db36def9, not stripp=
ed

I was hoping that this would be built for the architecture specified in loc=
al.conf for the toolchain, which is: SDKMACHINE ?=3D "x86_64"

I think that this architecture mismatch may be the root of the problem with=
 the LD_PRELOAD of pseudo.  I also would expect that the work directory wou=
ld be under x86_64-nativesdk-pokysdk-linux or x86_64-pokysdk-linux rather t=
han i586-poky-linux.

Do any of you Yocto/OE/bitbake experts out there know what I might be doing=
 wrong, or not doing, that causes this problem?

I have attached the output of the bitbake command, my local.conf file, the =
recipe, and config.log and config.status from the work directory for your v=
iewing pleasure.

Any help with this would be greatly appreciated.

-Jim-

